Copyright and attribution notes for the mcglmgraph package
==========================================================

The mcglmgraph package extends the Multivariate Covariance Generalized Linear
Models (MCGLM) framework created by Wagner Hugo Bonat and Bent Jorgensen.

The estimation methodology (second-order estimating functions, quasi-score and
Pearson estimating functions, sensitivity and variability matrices, and the
sandwich variance estimator) follows the MCGLM framework as documented in:

  Bonat, W. H. and Jorgensen, B. (2016). Multivariate covariance generalized
  linear models. Journal of the Royal Statistical Society: Series C, 65(5),
  649-675. <doi:10.1111/rssc.12145>

  Bonat, W. H. (2018). Multiple response variables regression models in R:
  the mcglm package. Journal of Statistical Software, 84(4), 1-30.
  <doi:10.18637/jss.v084.i04>

The mcglm package (GPL-3, Wagner Hugo Bonat) is the conceptual and reference
basis for the estimating-function engine. The mcglmgraph package is licensed
under GPL-3, consistent with the license of the framework it extends.

The graph-structured between-response parametrizations (Gaussian graphical
models, directed acyclic graphs via the modified Cholesky decomposition, and
structure learning) and all C++ kernels in src/ are original contributions of
Jose Evandeilton Lopes, developed during his doctoral research at the Graduate
Program in Numerical Methods in Engineering (PPGMNE) of the Federal University
of Parana (UFPR), under the supervision of Prof. Wagner Hugo Bonat.
